## Constructor arguments on ELF triples (the section 12 rows of 2026-10-26
## 'M22.b extended (Rust-found defects 2 and 4)' item 4 and 'M22.e extended
## (Rust-found defects 1-4, tests)'; ImplementationPlan.md 5.8.8 INIT
## entries, 5.9.9's constructor list, 5.9.10): glibc calls each
## '.init_array' entry as void (int argc, char **argv, char **envp), and Rust
## std's ARGV_INIT_ARRAY relies on it.
## - On linux-gnu MSIL triples a constructor in llvm.global_ctors or in an
##   '.init_array' slot whose type is void (i32, ptr, ptr), or a prefix of it
##   ((i32), (i32, ptr)), is called with argc and argv as '<msil>Main' passes
##   them to main and with the process environment for envp (libc's
##   environ, a data import from libc.so.6): llc -filetype=obj writes its
##   INIT entry, and msil-ld's object link, its LTO PE link, --lto-emit-asm
##   and whole-program text (llc, as clang -S) accept it and call it with as
##   many arguments as it takes;
## - any other parameter list stays the error
##   'global constructor '<c>' takes arguments, which MSIL does not pass',
##   and so does every constructor that takes arguments on windows-msvc
##   (MSVC's CRT calls '.CRT$XC*' entries without arguments, here an
##   llvm.global_ctors entry and a '.CRT$XCU' slot); llc reports it for
##   llvm.global_ctors in objects, msil-ld for a slot, the LTO code generator
##   for msil-ld's bitcode links.
## The environ import of a constructor that takes envp (section 12 row
## '5.9.10 amended (constructor arguments)' of 2026-10-26; 5.10.12, 5.10.14,
## 5.9.14): args3.ll never names environ, so the output gets the data-import
## field '<msil>environ', imported from the first native data definition of
## environ in link order:
## - --print-imports prints the same lines as for env.ll, which reads environ
##   itself (environ as data, and the helper's dlopen and dlsym, from
##   libc.so.6, and libc.so.6's version floor), in the object link, the LTO
##   PE link and --lto-emit-asm; -Map lists libc.so.6!environ under Imports:
##   with the symbol '<msil>environ';
## - a library of another soname that defines environ (libfoo.so, built from
##   the same glibc.yaml object) serves the import: the image's P/Invokes and
##   data import name libfoo.so, and so does the --lto-emit-asm text (its
##   kind-1 !msil.imports operand), which names no libc.so.6;
## - with no native definition of environ, an msil-ld link (objects, the LTO
##   PE link, -shared and --lto-emit-asm) is the error
##   'global constructor '<c>' takes envp, but no native library of the link
##   defines 'environ'';
## - the same holds when llvm.global_ctors names an internal alias of the
##   constructor (alias.ll: @init_alias -> init3): under --lto-O0, which
##   keeps the alias, the LTO PE link and --lto-emit-asm agree, both the
##   error without a definition of environ and both importing environ, dlopen
##   and dlsym from libfoo.so with it (M22 review r2 finding 5; the error may
##   name the alias or the aliasee).
## Every main here takes no arguments, so no output gets the '<msil>argc' and
## '<msil>argv' trailer fields that obj-ctors-main-args.test covers (section 12
## row 'M22.b extended (defect 4) clarified').
## libc.so.6 is the glibc-like stub of Inputs/native/glibc.yaml, which
## defines environ.

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: yaml2obj --docnum=1 %S/Inputs/native/glibc.yaml -o libc.o
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libc.so.6 --version-script %S/Inputs/native/glibc-libc.map libc.o -o libc.so.6
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj args3.ll -o args3.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj args1.ll -o args1.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj args2.ll -o args2.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj slot.ll -o slot.o
# RUN: llvm-as args3.ll -o args3.bc
# RUN: llvm-as other.ll -o other.bc
# RUN: llvm-as four.ll -o four.bc
# RUN: llvm-as win.ll -o win.bc
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj winslot.ll -o winslot.o

# DEFINE: %{fc} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"
# DEFINE: %{listing} = %python %S/Inputs/shared/listing.py
# DEFINE: %{noargv} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not="'<msil>argc'" --implicit-check-not="'<msil>argv'"

## The object INIT entries and the calls.
